  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t),\\,{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\u27e9 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =|{e}^{t}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}\u2061t-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t+{cos}^{2}\u2061t+2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
